Subject: [PATCH] irqchip/gic-v3: clear inherited SPI pending state before enable

Adapted from machachu56/quest-kexec-q2 commit
9c96c192d4a4a80f95ba0013294977e85c6eae11, Quest2 patch0001.
Base kernel:6bde5fc06b252c97761bc0963dd13c1abcf377ab.

The matching common helper already disables and deactivates SPIs. Clear their
pending state after that helper, while the distributor is disabled. Do not
duplicate active-state clearing or touch private interrupts. This cannot quiesce
a peripheral that is still asserting a level interrupt, or establish DMA safety.
No watchdog, fixed RAM logging, SMMU bypass or failure suppression is imported.

diff --git a/drivers/irqchip/irq-gic-v3.c b/drivers/irqchip/irq-gic-v3.c
--- a/drivers/irqchip/irq-gic-v3.c
+++ b/drivers/irqchip/irq-gic-v3.c
@@ -516,6 +516,14 @@ static void __init gic_dist_init(void)
 	gic_dist_config(base, gic_data.irq_nr, gic_dist_wait_for_rwp);
 
+	/*
+	 * The common helper has disabled and deactivated SPIs. Clear inherited
+	 * pending state before enabling the distributor. An asserted level
+	 * source can remain pending; its producer still needs proper shutdown.
+	 */
+	for (i = 32; i < gic_data.irq_nr; i += 32)
+		writel_relaxed(~0, base + GICD_ICPENDR + i / 8);
+
 	/* Enable distributor with ARE, Group1 */
 	writel_relaxed(GICD_CTLR_ARE_NS | GICD_CTLR_ENABLE_G1A | GICD_CTLR_ENABLE_G1,
 		       base + GICD_CTLR);
 
